{
  "title": "Independent layout and mask draws reproduce the endpoint-fixation power loss",
  "statement": "Replicate the 160-line, 1,500-book pilot and test whether its endpoint-locking power curve persists across three independently sampled public line layouts and independently seeded nested masks and outcome simulations. Compare the exact pilot before pooling results.",
  "program": "J",
  "check": "Compare all eight planted final rates under 0%, 50%, 90% and 100% fixed line endings. Confirm the baseline result matches the merged pilot, report per-seed power and uncertainty, and verify that 100% fixation produces no rejections by construction.",
  "on_path": true,
  "hard": false,
  "findings": "The unchanged base plan reproduced every stored pilot rejection count and interval. Across the three new layout/mask/simulation seeds, at a 5% final rate and 1% interior rate, mean rejection probability was 0.713 (range 0.703\u20130.721) with no endpoints fixed, 0.370 (0.364\u20130.381) with half fixed, 0.037 (0.037\u20130.039) with 90% fixed, and 0 at full fixation. At a 10% final rate the corresponding means were 0.997, 0.889, 0.185 and 0. At the 1% null the mean rejection rate remained below alpha in every condition; fully fixed endpoints yielded zero rejections. The direction and scale of the power loss persisted across the three independent public layouts and masks.",
  "interpretation": "The pilot conclusion is robust over these sampled public layouts: endpoint-fixing nulls can sharply reduce power to detect a terminal effect. At a 5% final versus 1% interior rate, fixing 90% of endpoints reduced detection from about 71% to about 4%. The absolute 90%-fixed estimate varied by about 0.003 across these three alternate seeds. At complete fixation the exact conditional test is immobile and cannot reject by construction. This is a simulation sensitivity result for the stated model, layout family, and inclusive Poisson-binomial upper tail. It does not estimate power for the production F-001 ratio rule, its word-level shuffle, real manuscripts, or other effect-generating mechanisms.",
  "reproduction": "The original merged pilot is stored verbatim as python_source below. Run python -m vs fetch, then use the original plan plus three plan copies with (layout_seed, mask_seed, simulation_seed) (409,2402,20261127), (410,2403,20261128), and (411,2404,20261129). Execute python run_replicates.py from the repository root with Python 3.12. The run script uses null_power.run unchanged and reports all four result objects in full_results. The base plan reproduces the stored pilot; all masks are nested from one independently seeded shuffle within each plan.",
  "python_source": "\"\"\"Calibrate a line-final permutation test while fixing selected endings.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom math import sqrt\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport random\nfrom statistics import median\nimport sys\n\nfrom vs import corpus\n\n\ndef upper_tail(lines):\n    \"\"\"Exact inclusive tail for independent terminal draws conditional on each line total.\"\"\"\n    observed = 0\n    distribution = [1.0]\n    for eligible, positives, final in lines:\n        if positives in (0, eligible):\n            assert final == (positives == eligible)\n            continue\n        observed += final\n        probability = positives / eligible\n        distribution.append(0.0)\n        for k in range(len(distribution) - 1, 0, -1):\n            distribution[k] = (\n                distribution[k] * (1 - probability) + distribution[k - 1] * probability\n            )\n        distribution[0] *= 1 - probability\n    return min(1.0, sum(distribution[observed:]))\n\n\ndef wilson(successes, trials):\n    p = successes / trials\n    z = 1.959963984540054\n    scale = 1 + z * z / trials\n    centre = (p + z * z / (2 * trials)) / scale\n    radius = z * sqrt(p * (1 - p) / trials + z * z / (4 * trials * trials)) / scale\n    return [max(0.0, centre - radius), min(1.0, centre + radius)]\n\n\ndef public_line_lengths(plan):\n    public_training, _ = corpus.split_pages('practice', 'zl')\n    lengths = [\n        len(line.words)\n        for page in public_training if page.language == 'B'\n        for line in page.lines if line.unit == 'P' and len(line.words) >= 3\n    ]\n    return random.Random(plan['layout_seed']).choices(lengths, k=plan['lines_per_book'])\n\n\ndef run(plan):\n    lengths = public_line_lengths(plan)\n    order = list(range(len(lengths)))\n    random.Random(plan['mask_seed']).shuffle(order)\n    masks = {\n        str(fraction): sorted(order[round(fraction * len(lengths)):])\n        for fraction in plan['locked_fractions']\n    }\n    rng = random.Random(plan['simulation_seed'])\n    trials = plan['books_per_rate']\n    rows = {}\n    for final_rate in plan['final_rates']:\n        counts = dict.fromkeys(masks, 0)\n        for _ in range(trials):\n            lines = []\n            for length in lengths:\n                interior = sum(rng.random() < plan['interior_rate'] for _ in range(length - 2))\n                final = rng.random() < final_rate\n                lines.append((length - 1, interior + final, final))\n            for locked, free_indices in masks.items():\n                counts[locked] += upper_tail(lines[i] for i in free_indices) <= plan['alpha']\n        rows[str(final_rate)] = {\n            locked: {\n                'rejections': count,\n                'rate': count / trials,\n                'wilson_95': wilson(count, trials),\n            }\n            for locked, count in counts.items()\n        }\n    assert all(row['1']['rejections'] == 0 for row in rows.values())\n    return {\n        'plan': plan,\n        'layout': {'minimum': min(lengths), 'median': median(lengths), 'maximum': max(lengths)},\n        'power': rows,\n    }\n\n\ndef main():\n    assert upper_tail([]) == 1.0\n    assert abs(upper_tail([(5, 1, True)]) - .2) < 1e-12\n    assert abs(upper_tail([(5, 1, True), (4, 1, True)]) - .05) < 1e-12\n    assert upper_tail([(3, 3, True), (2, 0, False)]) == 1.0\n    plan = json.loads(Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text())\n    result = run(plan)\n    Path(sys.argv[2]).write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2) + '\\n')\n    for rate, fractions in result['power'].items():\n        print(rate, {fraction: round(row['rate'], 3) for fraction, row in fractions.items()})\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
